## 4. Proposed Changes

### 4.1 New Helper: `findArchivedSessionForIssue()`

A general-purpose function to search archived sessions by issue ID and agent name. This generalizes the pattern from `findOpenCodeSessionIds()` but returns AO session metadata instead of agent-internal session IDs.

**Location:** `packages/core/src/session-manager.ts` (alongside `findOpenCodeSessionIds`)

**Must reuse existing helpers** — `listArchivedSessionIds()`, `readArchivedMetadataRaw()`, and `sortSessionIdsForReuse()` — instead of raw filesystem scanning. The original approach of using `file.indexOf("_")` to split archive filenames is **broken** for session IDs containing underscores (e.g., `app_v2_2025-06-15T12-00-00-000Z` → `indexOf("_")` returns 3 → extracts `"app"` instead of `"app_v2"`). The existing helpers use regex `/^([a-zA-Z0-9_-]+)_\d/` which handles this correctly.

```typescript
function findArchivedSessionForIssue(
  sessionsDir: string,
  issueId: string,
  agentName: string,
): { sessionId: string; raw: Record<string, string> } | null {
  // sortSessionIdsForReuse gives most-recent-first ordering,
  // so the first match is the most recent session for this issue.
  for (const sessionId of sortSessionIdsForReuse(listArchivedSessionIds(sessionsDir))) {
    const raw = readArchivedMetadataRaw(sessionsDir, sessionId);
    if (!raw) continue;
    if (raw["issue"] === issueId && raw["agent"] === agentName) {
      return { sessionId, raw };
    }
  }
  return null;
}
```

### 4.2 Modify `spawn()` to Attempt Resume

In `spawn()`, after building `agentLaunchConfig` and before creating the runtime (around line 1058-1060), add a resume attempt:

```typescript
// --- Attempt to resume previous session for same issue ---
let launchCommand: string;
let resumedFromSession: string | null = null;

const respawnStrategy = project.workerRespawnStrategy ?? "resume";

if (
  respawnStrategy !== "fresh" &&
  spawnConfig.issueId &&
  plugins.agent.getRestoreCommand
) {
  const archived = findArchivedSessionForIssue(
    sessionsDir,
    spawnConfig.issueId,
    selection.agentName,
  );

  if (archived) {
    const archivedSession = metadataToSession(archived.sessionId, archived.raw, spawnConfig.projectId);
    archivedSession.workspacePath = workspacePath; // Use current worktree, not archived one

    try {
      const restoreCmd = await plugins.agent.getRestoreCommand(archivedSession, project);
      if (restoreCmd) {
        launchCommand = restoreCmd;
        resumedFromSession = archived.sessionId;
        log.info(`Resuming conversation from archived session ${archived.sessionId} for issue ${spawnConfig.issueId}`);
      }
    } catch (err) {
      log.warn(`Failed to build restore command from archived session ${archived.sessionId}: ${err}`);
    }
  }
}

if (!launchCommand) {
  launchCommand = plugins.agent.getLaunchCommand(agentLaunchConfig);
}
```

### 4.3 Context Injection Fallback

When native resume isn't possible (agent doesn't support `getRestoreCommand()`, or it returned `null`), inject a context summary into the prompt. This is the universal fallback for all agents.

**New helper function** in `session-manager.ts` or a new file `session-context-builder.ts`:

```typescript
async function buildPreviousSessionContext(
  archivedRaw: Record<string, string>,
  workspacePath: string,
): Promise<string | null> {
  const parts: string[] = [];
  parts.push("## Previous Session Context");
  parts.push(`A previous worker session worked on this same issue and ended with status: ${archivedRaw["status"] ?? "unknown"}.`);

  // Agent-generated summary
  if (archivedRaw["summary"]) {
    parts.push(`\n### Agent Summary\n${archivedRaw["summary"]}`);
  }

  // Git commits on the branch
  const branch = archivedRaw["branch"];
  if (branch && existsSync(workspacePath)) {
    try {
      const { stdout } = await execAsync(
        `git -C ${shellEscape(workspacePath)} log --oneline ${shellEscape(branch)} --not origin/main -- 2>/dev/null`
      );
      if (stdout.trim()) {
        const commits = stdout.trim().split("\n").slice(0, 20);
        parts.push(`\n### Commits Made\n${commits.map(c => `- ${c}`).join("\n")}`);
      }
    } catch { /* best effort */ }
  }

  // PR info
  if (archivedRaw["pr"]) {
    parts.push(`\nA PR was opened: ${archivedRaw["pr"]}. Check its status and review comments before continuing.`);
  }

  parts.push(`\n### Instructions\nDo NOT start over from scratch. Review the previous work and continue from where it left off. If the previous approach had issues, learn from them and try a different approach.`);

  // Only return context if we have something meaningful beyond the header
  if (!archivedRaw["summary"] && parts.length <= 3) return null;

  return parts.join("\n");
}
```

**Integration into `spawn()`** — extends the resume logic:

```typescript
// After the getRestoreCommand() attempt fails or is unavailable:
if (!launchCommand && respawnStrategy !== "fresh" && archived) {
  const context = await buildPreviousSessionContext(archived.raw, workspacePath);
  if (context) {
    // Prepend context to the issue prompt
    agentLaunchConfig.prompt = `${context}\n\n---\n\n${composedPrompt}`;
  }
  launchCommand = plugins.agent.getLaunchCommand(agentLaunchConfig);
}

if (!launchCommand) {
  launchCommand = plugins.agent.getLaunchCommand(agentLaunchConfig);
}
```

### 4.4 Configuration

The **user** decides the respawn strategy — it's a per-project setting in `agent-orchestrator.yaml`, following the same pattern as the existing `orchestratorSessionStrategy` (`config.ts:168-169`).

```yaml
# agent-orchestrator.yaml
projects:
  my-app:
    repo: owner/repo
    path: /path/to/repo
    workerRespawnStrategy: "resume"   # or "context-inject" or "fresh"
```

**Add to `ProjectConfig`** in `types.ts`:

```typescript
/** Strategy for handling previous sessions when spawning for the same issue.
 * - "resume" (default): try getRestoreCommand(), fall back to context injection, then fresh
 * - "context-inject": don't resume agent conversation, but inject context summary into prompt
 * - "fresh": always start fresh (current behavior, no change)
 */
workerRespawnStrategy?: "resume" | "context-inject" | "fresh";
```

**Add to `ProjectConfigSchema`** in `config.ts`:

```typescript
workerRespawnStrategy: z.enum(["resume", "context-inject", "fresh"]).optional(),
```

### 4.5 Track Lineage in Metadata

Add `resumedFrom` to the metadata written by `spawn()`:

```typescript
writeMetadata(sessionsDir, sessionId, {
  // ... existing fields ...
  resumedFrom: resumedFromSession,  // Session ID we resumed from, or undefined
});
```

This creates a lineage chain: `app-3` → resumedFrom `app-2` → resumedFrom `app-1`.

### 4.6 OpenCode `getRestoreCommand()` (Optional)

Since OpenCode already has session reuse via `--session` in `getLaunchCommand()`, a `getRestoreCommand()` implementation could simply delegate:

```typescript
async getRestoreCommand(session, project) {
  const opencodeSessionId = asValidOpenCodeSessionId(session.metadata?.opencodeSessionId);
  if (!opencodeSessionId) return null;

  // Delegate to getLaunchCommand with the session ID injected
  // This ensures the --session flag is included
  return this.getLaunchCommand({
    ...config,
    projectConfig: {
      ...project,
      agentConfig: { ...project.agentConfig, opencodeSessionId },
    },
  });
}
```

This makes OpenCode work through the restore path without any special-casing in `spawn()`.

