## Bug

Session card in the dashboard kanban view blinks/flashes when the card's attention level oscillates between zones on consecutive SSE snapshot pushes. The `kanban-card-enter` entrance animation (`opacity: 0 → 1`, `translateY: 8px → 0`) replays each time the card unmounts from one column and remounts in another, creating a visible flash every ~5 seconds.

**Discord thread:** https://discord.com/channels/1484917231245856808/1491735678156013588/1496254650737885457
**Reported by:** @Ashish
**Analyzed against:** `59f66f4` (main)

## Screenshot

![blinking card in ACTION column](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ComposioHQ/agent-orchestrator/issue-assets-blinking-card/.issue-assets/blinking-card-screenshot.png)

## Reproduction

1. Have a session whose attention level is borderline between two zones (e.g., `working` vs `action` in simple mode)
2. Observe the card in the dashboard kanban view
3. Card blinks every SSE update cycle (~5s) as it moves between columns

## Root Cause

The `kanban-card-enter` CSS class is unconditionally applied to every `SessionCard`:

**`packages/web/src/components/SessionCard.tsx:459`**
```tsx
className={cn(
  "session-card kanban-card-enter border",  // ← always applied
  cardFrameClass,
  accentClass,
  ...
)}
```

**`packages/web/src/app/globals.css:784-812`**
```css
.kanban-card-enter {
  animation: card-enter 0.2s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) both;
}

@keyframes card-enter {
  from {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(8px);
  }
  to {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }
}
```

The `animation-fill-mode: both` means the card starts at `opacity: 0` before the animation plays. When React unmounts the card from one `AttentionZone` column and remounts it in another (due to the attention level changing), the browser treats it as a new DOM element and replays the animation from scratch.

**The oscillation path:**

1. `useSessionEvents` reducer processes SSE snapshot → updates `status`/`activity`/`lastActivityAt` on session objects (`useSessionEvents.ts:62-73`)
2. New session object reference → `displaySessions` useMemo recomputes (`Dashboard.tsx:202-205`)
3. `grouped` useMemo recomputes → calls `getAttentionLevel(session, attentionZones)` (`Dashboard.tsx:234`)
4. If the returned attention level differs from previous, the session moves to a different column
5. Card with `key={session.id}` unmounts from old column's `AttentionZone`, mounts in new one
6. `kanban-card-enter` animation replays → visible opacity 0→1 flash

**Why the level oscillates:** The session card is shown in the ACTION column (simple mode collapses respond+review → action) with status "working". This suggests the client-side `getAttentionLevel` computation produces a non-working level (likely due to stale `lifecycle` data from initial SSR that still has `sessionState: "needs_input"` or similar), while the actual session status is "working". On each SSE push, the session data partially updates, potentially causing the computed level to flip between "working" and the stale-driven level.

Note: `SessionCard` calls `getAttentionLevel(session)` without mode (defaults to `"detailed"`) at line 129, while Dashboard grouping passes `attentionZones` mode. This means the card's internal styling level and the column placement level can disagree.

## Fix

**Option A (recommended): One-shot entrance animation.** Track whether the card has already played its entrance animation using a ref, then remove the `kanban-card-enter` class after the first play. This preserves the nice entrance effect for genuinely new cards while preventing re-trigger on column moves.

```tsx
const [hasEntered, setHasEntered] = useState(false);
useEffect(() => { setHasEntered(true); }, []);

// In className:
cn(
  "session-card border",
  !hasEntered && "kanban-card-enter",  // only on first mount
  ...
)
```

**Option B: CSS-only fix.** Use `animation-fill-mode: forwards` and set the card's natural opacity to 1. This doesn't prevent the animation from replaying on remount but eliminates the opacity-0 start state that makes it visible.

**Option C: Prevent remounting.** Don't re-key cards when they change columns. This is a larger architectural change — would require all cards to exist in a flat list with absolute positioning.

## Impact

- Visual distraction for dashboard users monitoring working sessions
- Makes it harder to read card content during the flash
- Affects any session whose attention level is computed differently between SSE updates

## Bug Report

### Summary
When AO sessions are killed without going through proper teardown, the worktree plugin's `destroy()` method falls back to `rmSync` which deletes the worktree directory but leaves the `.git/worktrees/<id>/` registration intact. The next `ao start` then collides on either the path or the branch.

### Root Cause Analysis

**Original author:** Prateek (`925a7aae9`, Feb 14 2026, PR #2 — initial plugin implementation)
**Secondary contributor:** Ashish Huddar (`f3ce113c4`, Apr 21 2026, PR #1343 — multi-project storage)

The `destroy()` method was written in the very first commit that implemented the worktree plugin (PR #2). The fallback `rmSync` in the `catch` block was a reasonable "best effort" cleanup at the time, but it was never followed up with `git worktree prune` to clean up the stale registration in `.git/worktrees/`. The code has survived untouched through all subsequent refactors.

Ashish later added `clearStaleWorktreePath()` (PR #1343) which has a similar pattern but with a partial guard — it calls `git worktree prune` + `isRegisteredWorktree` before `rmSync`. However, if the prune itself fails silently, the guard is bypassed and the same stale registration issue occurs.

### Affected Code

**Bug location #1 — `destroy()` fallback** (`packages/plugins/workspace-worktree/src/index.ts`, lines 192–215):
```typescript
async destroy(workspacePath: string): Promise<void> {
  try {
    const gitCommonDir = await git(workspacePath, "rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-common-dir");
    const repoPath = resolve(gitCommonDir, "..");
    await git(repoPath, "worktree", "remove", "--force", workspacePath);
  } catch {
    // BUG: rmSync removes directory but leaves .git/worktrees/<id>/ registration
    if (existsSync(workspacePath)) {
      rmSync(workspacePath, { recursive: true, force: true });
    }
  }
},
```

**Bug location #2 — `clearStaleWorktreePath()`** (`packages/plugins/workspace-worktree/src/index.ts`, lines 84–100):
```typescript
async function clearStaleWorktreePath(repoPath: string, worktreePath: string): Promise<void> {
  try {
    await git(repoPath, "worktree", "prune");
  } catch { /* Best-effort prune — failure swallowed silently */ }

  if (await isRegisteredWorktree(repoPath, worktreePath)) {
    throw new Error(`Worktree path "${worktreePath}" already exists and is still registered with git`);
  }
  // If prune above failed, this rmSync leaves stale registration
  rmSync(worktreePath, { recursive: true, force: true });
}
```

### All Code Paths That Trigger This

| Path | Trigger | File |
|---|---|---|
| `ao session kill` | User kills session | `session-manager.ts:2072` |
| `ao session cleanup` | Stale session cleanup | `session-manager.ts:2211` |
| SIGTERM/Ctrl+C | Graceful shutdown (10s timeout!) | `start.ts:2280` |
| PR merge auto-cleanup | Lifecycle detects merged PR | `lifecycle-manager.ts:1763` |
